diff --git a/docs/TESTING_PERFORMANCE.md b/docs/TESTING_PERFORMANCE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ab03c15
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/TESTING_PERFORMANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# RSpec performance notes
+
+These measurements cover only `spec/models`. System, streaming, and request specs are intentionally excluded, as are factory changes during this optimization phase. Use the same seed for before/after comparisons and do not run multiple spec directories in one profiling command.
+
+## Model spec baseline (2026-11-23)
+
+Command:
+
+```shell
+bundle exec rspec spec/models --format progress --profile 30 --seed 12533
+```
+
+| Run | Examples | RSpec time | Wall time |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Baseline, globally inline Sidekiq | 1795 | 176.9s | 180.361s |
+| Model specs use fake Sidekiq plus shared setup | 1795 | 99.31s | 102.925s |
+
+Both runs completed with zero failures. The final run is 43.9% faster by RSpec time and 42.9% faster by wall time.
+
+## Findings
+
+- EventProf measured 3,908 inline Sidekiq events taking 63.321s, or 29.33% of the instrumented run. Common model callbacks enqueue webhook and mail-related workers while records are fabricated. Model specs now use Sidekiq's fake mode by default; examples that assert actual mail delivery opt into `sidekiq: :inline`.
+- RSpec Dissect measured 111.636s of setup out of 140.242s under fake Sidekiq mode. The largest avoidable setup costs came from recreating the same records for each example in `AccountStatusesCleanupPolicy`, `TagFeed`, and `Form::Import`. These specs now use `let_it_be`/`before_all` for stable database graphs and `refind: true` for fresh Active Record instances in each example. Data mutations remain inside each example's transaction.
+- The first fake-Sidekiq pass ran in 131.8s but found three examples whose assertions depend on mail delivery executing inline. They are isolated with metadata rather than changing their assertions or the global mode for unrelated specs.
+- Sidekiq mode for non-model spec types is unchanged. A model context hook also sets fake mode before `let_it_be` setup, because `before_all` runs before per-example hooks.
+- Factory definitions were not changed. Factory setup remains a suitable future optimization area after the setup-level pass.
+
+## Reprofiling
+
+Profile repeated setup:
+
+```shell
+RD_PROF=1 RD_PROF_TOP=30 RD_PROF_LET_TOP=5 \
+  bundle exec rspec spec/models --require ./spec/rails_helper --require test_prof \
+  --format progress --seed 12533
+```
+
+Profile SQL and Sidekiq events when investigating job-mode costs:
+
+```shell
+EVENT_PROF='sql.active_record,sidekiq.inline' \
+  EVENT_PROF_EXAMPLES=1 EVENT_PROF_TOP=20 \
+  bundle exec rspec spec/models --require ./spec/rails_helper --require test_prof \
+  --format progress --seed 12533
+```
+
+Instrumented runs have profiling overhead; compare final uninstrumented timings for the speed target. After the shared-setup pass, the largest remaining groups by RSpec time are `Trends::Statuses`, `Status::ThreadingConcern`, and `MediaAttachment`. Request specs still need a separate baseline and optimization pass.
